# tools/ales_drive_witness.rish — the hard-clip drive: a pre-gain into ALES49's ceiling, opening the DRIVE family (ALES78).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES78.
# Design read: active-designing/20260814-204949_fill-ales78-lotus-hard-clip-drive.md
# Stands on: lotus/limit.rye (ALES49 — the ceiling law `pin to sign(x)·ceil`, reused over the BOOSTED sample rather than the dry one);
# lotus/fader.rye (ALES6/ALES8 — the num/den gain in the i64 accumulator, the drive's pre-gain); lotus/tremolo.rye (ALES74 — the amplitude kin
# whose unity boundary this rung reads in reverse); lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip, sample_min/max, the one true saturate).
#
# lotus/drive.rye opens the DRIVE family beside the EQ, dynamics, and modulation families. DRIVE IS PRE-GAIN INTO ALES49's CEILING: it is
# ALES74's tremolo read in reverse — where the tremolo FORBIDS the gain past unity so its saturate stays a no-op, the drive INVITES the gain
# past unity and lets the ceiling catch the overflow, and that caught overflow IS the harmonic voice (y[i] = pin(x[i]·num/den, ±ceil), ALES6's
# i64 gain into ALES49's pin). The selftest proves it: a unity drive at the rail is the identity; a ×4 drive into a low ceiling clips so the
# ceiling is never crossed and every sign is held (the flat top where harmonics are born — the crux); a hand-computed ×3/2 drive matches
# exactly; the clipper is ODD, drive(−x) = −drive(x), so a symmetric input yields odd harmonics; an EXTREME drive squares the wave (every
# non-zero sample pins, zeros stay silent); the span discipline holds (only [start, count) changes); a zero denominator / below-unity gain /
# oversized numerator refuses BadGain, a zero or over-rail ceiling BadCeiling, a span past the end BadRange, each leaving the clip untouched.
# The pin lands every output in [−ceil, ceil] ⊆ the i16 rail BEFORE the write, so the clip is the pin and the saturate a documented no-op.
# Purely local — one multiply, one divide, one sign-carried pin per sample; no delay line, no anti-aliasing, no network, no keys, no funds,
# no real device, no real sample rate.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_drive_witness.rish

say "ales-drive: Language EN — the modulation family closed at ALES77 (delay, amplitude, position, each turned by an LFO). This rung opens the DRIVE family, which turns SHAPE: a drive boosts a signal hard and lets a ceiling catch what overflows, and the flat top of the clipped wave is where its harmonics are born — the grit of an overdriven amp, the crunch of a fuzz. Hard clip first, because every richer drive (a soft knee, a wavefolder, an asymmetric tube) rests on it."
say "ales-drive: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively as a recognition: DRIVE IS PRE-GAIN INTO ALES49's CEILING, the mirror of ALES74's tremolo. Where the tremolo forbids the gain from crossing unity so its saturate stays a no-op, the drive invites the gain past unity and lets ALES49's ceiling catch what overflows — and that caught overflow IS the harmonic voice. No new gain arithmetic (ALES6's num/den, verbatim) and no new clip law (ALES49's sign-held pin, verbatim); only the ceiling now falls over the BOOSTED sample rather than the dry one."
say "ales-drive: Lens TAME — one mono clip of i16 PCM driven in place over a span; a drive gain is num/den with num ≥ den ≥ 1 (a drive boosts, never attenuates) and num ≤ max_drive_num, so the pre-gain x·num stays well inside i64; the pin lands every output in [−ceil, ceil] ⊆ [sample_min, sample_max] BEFORE the write, so the clip is the pin and the saturate a documented no-op; a zero denominator, a below-unity gain, or a numerator past the bound refuses BadGain (ALES74's unity boundary read in reverse), a ceiling outside [1, sample_max] BadCeiling, a span outside the samples BadRange, all before any write, the clip untouched on refusal; the drive is MEMORYLESS (every output depends only on its own input) and the clipper ODD (drive(−x) = −drive(x)); siloed to lotus/, the gain a rational and the ceiling a magnitude in sample units, no delay line, no snapshot, no anti-aliasing, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker, no sample rate."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/drive"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/drive.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-drive: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/drive.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-drive: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-drive: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-drive' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-drive: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-drive line"
